The intersection of two sets includes the elements that are common to both sets.

\[

\begin{array}{l}

B \cap C=\{0,6,12\} \\

A \cap(B \cap C)=\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6\} \cap\{0,6,12\} \\

A \cap(B \cap C)=\{0,6\} \\

A \cap(B \cap C)=\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6\} \cap\{0,6,12\}=\{0,6\}

\end{array}

\nonumber \]
